    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class in the suite, and it passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`). The implementation is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the daily owner-creation limit so that creating an owner is rejected with **429 Too Many Requests** once 100 or more owners already share the same `registrationDate`.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`DailyOwnerLimitExceededException.java`** (new) \u2014 a `RuntimeException` in the `rest.advice` package carrying the `registrationDate`, mirroring the existing `OwnerCityCapacityExceededException` pattern.\n\n2. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 in `addOwner`, after the registration date is defaulted to today, added a `rejectDailyLimitReached(owner.getRegistrationDate())` guard. The new helper counts existing owners whose `registrationDate` equals the new owner's date and throws when the count is `>= MAX_OWNERS_PER_DAY` (100).\n\n3. **`ExceptionControllerAdvice.java`** \u2014 added an `@ExceptionHandler` for the new exception returning `HttpStatus.TOO_MANY_REQUESTS` (429) with a `ProblemDetail`, consistent with the other owner-rule handlers, plus a matching `ERROR_RATE_LIMIT` message constant.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreRejectsOverDailyLimit` (creates 100 owners dated today, expects the 101st to be rejected with 429) passes, and the full suite is green.",
